    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10-a9">

                <pb facs="0109" n="17" sameAs="frus:frus1899/pg17"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 9.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herdliska to Aaron Kenig</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-06-16"><hi rendition="#italic">June 16,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your note of the 24th of May,
                    1898, from Hartford, Conn., making inquiry as to the progress of your case, the
                    minister <pb facs="0110" n="18" xml:id="pg18"/> of the United States of America
                    directs me to inform you that the facts in your case were presented in full, to
                    the Austro-Hungarian ministry of foreign affairs by this legation on the 9th of
                    March, 1898, with the request that an examination into the question be made by
                    the proper authorities in order that justice might be done you, and that the
                    money that was taken from you and your American passport might be returned to
                    you.</p>
                <p>As soon as a decision is rendered by the Austro-Hungarian Government in your
                    case, it will at once be communicated to you through the Department of State at
                    Washington.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles V. Herdliska</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of Legation.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
